# THE RULE: a file the build READS is an asset and is committed; anything a tool WRITES is
# output and is not. The directory does not make that obvious on its own, so it is stated here.
#
#   art/            source art (renders, paintings, hand-drawn sprites) -- committed
#   *.json (root)   FITTED assets the build reads (angel-art, goat-art, quote-screen, ...) -- committed
#   iray.asm        generated, but committed ON PURPOSE: diffing it between commits shows what a JS
#                   change did to the machine code and the memory map. Both early layout bugs were
#                   invisible in the JS diff, so that churn earns its keep.

# ---- build output: `node build-iray.mjs` regenerates all of it ----
*.d64
!art/*.d64
# ...except THE game, committed so a visitor can play it without building
!lest-c64.d64
iray.prg
iray-c.prg
iray-charset.bin
# diagnostic builds (PX/PY/PA/SPIN/NORAY/...) emit here, so a throwaway start position never
# lands in the tracked iray.asm
iray.diag.asm
# compact.mjs's inputs and outputs. A stale copy of any of them would relayout the image against
# a build that no longer exists.
iray.aligned.json
iray.bufsizes.json
iray.hotloops.json
iray.reserve.json
iray.syms.json
iray.compact.asm
# one per resident level / removable wall, written by the build's own sub-builds
.lvl*-tables.json
.wall*-tables.json
# diagnostic dumps
cellscan.json
orbdiag.json
face-extra.json
# charset-plan.json is TRACKED. It looks derived and it is not: it is the k-medians fit over a
# 2M-position scan of a shape-rich maze, canonical input to every build, and no level's map is an
# input to it. Untracked, a clean clone would refit the charset against whatever map was built.
# Regenerate deliberately with:
#   CELLSCAN=1 CELLSTEP=0.2 CELLANG=1 node build-iray.mjs && node charsetgen.mjs

# ---- pictures at the top level are tool output: previews, ladders, screenshots, frames ----
# (art lives in art/; fit-angel's previews regenerate with `node fit-angel.mjs art/TMP-3.d64 hangl1`)
/*.png
/*.gif
# c64pic's picture for the end scene (see tools/endscene.mjs for the recipe)
/tree.kla

# ---- reference material that is not ours to publish (photographs of real objects) ----
art/ref/

# ---- tools ----
tools/node_modules/
tools/package-lock.json
tools/.ship/

# ---- local only ----
.claude/
.DS_Store
CLEANUP-REVIEW.md
loader-v194.zip
krill/loader-rt-c64.prg
*.swp
